<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Twenty-third Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">837 BCE – 735 BCE (approx.) · capital Thebes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A rival Libyan line of kings in Upper Egypt, born from the civil wars that broke up the Twenty-second Dynasty.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 837 BCE, amid conflict in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-second-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-second Dynasty of Egypt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedubast-i">Pedubast I</a> proclaimed himself king and was recognised at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manetho">Manetho</a> linked the dynasty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanis">Tanis</a>, while earlier scholars placed it at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-el-muqdam">Leontopolis</a>; many Egyptologists now see it as a mainly Theban and Upper Egyptian line, but its extent is debated.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dynasty shared power with the Bubastite kings and local Libyan chiefs, each controlling cities and temples. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osorkon-iii">Osorkon III</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takelot-iii">Takelot III</a> ruled as co-regents and placed family members as high priests and as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gods-wife-of-amun">God's Wife of Amun</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>. Royal monuments are few, but Theban inscriptions record <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> flood levels and priestly appointments by year of each king.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 735 BCE <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> passed under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shepenupet-i">Shepenupet I</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osorkon-iii">Osorkon III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gods-wife-of-amun">God's Wife of Amun</a>, adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amenirdis-i">Amenirdis I</a>, sister of the Kushite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piye">Piye</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudamun">Rudamun's</a> line ended as minor rulers, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iuput-ii">Iuput II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-el-muqdam">Leontopolis</a> submitted to Piye.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/twenty-third-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Twenty-third Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="592"><figcaption>Image: Aoineko · CC BY-SA 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egypte_louvre_054.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>837 BCE – 735 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thebes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pedubast I, Osorkon III, Takelot III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Twenty-third Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-786&amp;focus=twenty-third-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Twenty-third Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5543 1232 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Twenty-third Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5863 1488L5817 1318M5863 1488L5862 1746"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5817 1318h0M5862 1746h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5863 1488h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5863 1488h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thebes. <a href="/atlas?year=-786&amp;focus=twenty-third-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
